e might want to raise concerns about crew cooperation and ask for more info. However we need to give a recommendation now. Could we say we still recommend B but want more info? The instruction: \"state or clearly imply your current hiring recommendation\". So we can say we still recommend B, but we need more evidence on crew cooperation. Provide evidence: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Concern: pretentious, wrong tone, weak memory for numbers, grumpy, uncooperative. Compare with others: A has leadership but not open to new ideas, show-off; C quick decisions but egocentric, not willing to further education; D responsibility but know-it-all, hot temper. So B still best overall.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: I still recommend Candidate B, citing strengths, acknowledging concerns, comparing with others. Then METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate B.\n\nProceed."}
